design:
Types to add (all behind cfg(feature=mdn)):

Mdn { for_email_id: Option<Id>, subject: Option<String>, text_body: Option<String>, include_original_message: bool (default false), reporting_ua: Option<String>, disposition: Disposition, mdn_gateway: Option<String> (server-set), original_recipient: Option<String> (server-set), final_recipient: Option<String>, original_message_id: Option<String> (server-set), error: Option<Vec<String>> (server-set), extension_fields: Option<HashMap<String,String>> }
All serde names camelCase. include_original_message defaults to false — use #[serde(default)].

Disposition { action_mode: ActionMode, sending_mode: SendingMode, type_: DispositionType }
Wire name for type_ is 'type' — use #[serde(rename = "type")].

ActionMode enum: ManualAction ("manual-action"), AutomaticAction ("automatic-action")
SendingMode enum: MdnSentManually ("mdn-sent-manually"), MdnSentAutomatically ("mdn-sent-automatically")
DispositionType enum: Deleted, Dispatched, Displayed, Processed — all lowercase in wire format. These are case-insensitive in RFC 8098 but MUST be lowercase per draft §2 (MDN/parse must convert).

MdnSendRequest { account_id: Id, identity_id: Id, send: HashMap<Id,Mdn>, on_success_update_email: Option<HashMap<Id,serde_json::Value>> }
MdnSendResponse { account_id: Id, sent: Option<HashMap<Id,Mdn>>, not_sent: Option<HashMap<Id,SetError>> }

MdnParseRequest { account_id: Id, blob_ids: Vec<Id> }
MdnParseResponse { account_id: Id, parsed: Option<HashMap<Id,Mdn>>, not_parsable: Option<Vec<Id>>, not_found: Option<Vec<Id>> }

MdnSetErrorType variants (extends base SetErrorType): MdnAlreadySent, ForbiddenFrom — plus existing notFound, forbidden, overQuota, tooLarge, rateLimit, invalidProperties.

JMAP_MDN_URI const = "urn:ietf:params:jmap:mdn"

Capability: empty object both at server and account level — just a unit struct that serializes as {}.
